{"duration_api_ms":185218,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"bc61f665-ce67-4468-830c-c8baddd1e865","total_cost_usd":0.25254,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16539,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":18638,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":12437},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16539,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":18638,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16539,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16539},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":18638,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16539,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.25254,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":12437,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The feasible front is a one-dimensional ridge at the corner D~3.385, bluntness 1.2, cone 70, running in flight_path_angle from -1.5 (flux 227k W/m2, T 417.9 K) to -3.5703 (flux 274.6k, T 391.1 K). Three limits pin that corner. max_g<=12 caps steepness at gamma ~ -3.5703. Heatshield mass fraction caps D at ~3.3852, and its margin is independent of gamma. The aero surrogate and geometry limit bluntness to <=1.2 and cone to >=~69.8 at this D. Every other region I have seen is dominated. HV has moved by less than 1e-4 per round since round 3. The only remaining gains are a slightly larger D (a tiny dominance improvement at every gamma) and denser sampling along the ridge.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-948029610632 to C-105ca6c5af01: at D=3.385, b=1.2, cone=70, flux rises 227k to 275k while T falls 417.9 to 391.1 K as gamma goes from -1.5 to -3.57. The curve is smooth and convex (dT/dF about -0.73 near -1.5, about -0.41 near -3.5).\",\"Mass-fraction margin is 0.0001449 at D=3.385, 0.003097 at D=3.38 and 2.677e-05 at D=3.3852. That is linear with slope ~0.59 per m, and it is identical at every gamma. It extrapolates to zero at D~3.38525, so D=3.38523 should be feasible.\",\"C-956957ec60d4, C-7112b6b29bcf and C-14444dd6b10a: lowering bluntness below 1.2 violates mass fraction and raises flux. C-05edbf22eaa2, C-3d41ce848a30 and C-3136d3bd2588 (b>1.2) and C-e0197c1bd7dc and C-7db223121090 (cone<70 at b=1.2) fail on geometry or surrogate extrapolation. The corner cannot be moved.\",\"C-6041504dc2c9: D=3.3 gives flux 283k and T 393.3 K at gamma -3.5, worse than D=3.3852 (272.9k, 391.76 K). Larger D helps and smaller D does not.\",\"C-105ca6c5af01 has g margin 1.486e-05 at gamma -3.5703 and D=3.3852. With dg/dgamma ~1.65 per deg, gamma -3.5704 is right at the g=12 limit.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak g is set almost entirely by gamma, so g<=12 fixes the steep end at ~-3.5703. Shield mass fraction scales with D^2, which fixes D at ~3.3852 for the blunt 70-degree cone. Larger D and higher Cd give a lower ballistic coefficient, so peak heating occurs higher and both flux and T fall slightly. Shallower gamma lowers flux but lengthens the pulse and raises T, which produces the convex ridge. With D at its limit, the front can only be improved by using D=3.38523 (about -25 W/m2 and -0.004 K at each gamma) and by adding points along gamma. All proposals are corner designs (b=1.2, cone=70) with D=3.38523, varying only gamma. One proposal probes gamma=-3.5704 at D=3.3852.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Predictions come from interpolating the D=3.385 ridge and applying a small D correction estimated from two nearby D values, so flux and T should be accurate to about 0.1%. The main risk is the two limit-hugging points: D=3.38523 (mass-fraction margin ~1e-5) and gamma=-3.5704 (g margin ~0). Either could come out infeasible. Expected HV gain is very small because the front is nearly saturated.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-948029610632\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow end of the ridge with D raised to 3.38523. It should slightly dominate C-948029610632.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38523,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":227190,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.86,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether the D increase gives a strict improvement at the extreme low-flux end and confirms the mass-fraction extrapolation.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-948029610632\",\"rationale\":\"Fills the gap between gamma -1.5 and -1.65 at the larger D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38523,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":228180,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.05,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds coverage along the low-flux end of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-948029610632\",\"rationale\":\"Fills the gap between -1.5 and -1.65.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38523,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.58},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":228770,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":416.55,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front densification.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-163399613c78\",\"rationale\":\"Fills the gap between -1.65 and -1.7.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38523,\"flight_path_angle_de